Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report the pending tx MSDU count in soc_dp_stats

The number of MSDUs handed to the hardware and not yet completed is what
the AQL charge in mac80211 is outstanding against, but nothing exports it,
so the driver-side occupancy cannot be compared against what mac80211
believes is pending.

Report it per pdev in soc_dp_stats, along with the capacity of the tx
descriptor idr, which holds one entry short of DP_TX_IDR_SIZE.

This is a backport of patch 3/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debugfs.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debugfs.c
index 977f945..575aa9b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debugfs.c
@@ -715,6 +715,23 @@ static ssize_t ath11k_debugfs_dump_soc_dp_stats(struct file *file,
 			 "\nMisc Transmit Failures: %d\n",
 			 atomic_read(&soc_stats->tx_err.misc_fail));
 
+	/* MSDUs handed to the hardware and not yet completed. The tx
+	 * descriptor idr holds one entry short of DP_TX_IDR_SIZE, so this is
+	 * also what the AQL charge in mac80211 is outstanding against.
+	 */
+	len += scnprintf(buf + len, size - len,
+			 "\nPending TX MSDUs (max %d):\n", DP_TX_IDR_SIZE - 1);
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
+		struct ath11k *ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
+
+		if (!ar)
+			continue;
+
+		len += scnprintf(buf + len, size - len, "pdev%d: %d\n",
+				 i, atomic_read(&ar->dp.num_tx_pending));
+	}
+
 	len += ath11k_debugfs_dump_soc_ring_bp_stats(ab, buf + len, size - len);
 
 	if (len > size)
